    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d568">

                <pb facs="0845" n="731" xml:id="pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1229a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Bolivia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Trueblood</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-24T13:00:00-04:00">June 24, 1931—1
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>24. Legation at Asuncion reported on 23d instant<anchor n="65" xml:id="d568-f1"/>
                    that a Bolivian note was delivered the previous day protesting against recent
                    statements of Paraguayan Chargé d’Affaires at Washington and requesting
                    rectification under threat to recall Minister at Asuncion. Cable adds that
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs is reported at his home indisposed but at the same
                    time drafted a reply which was due to be delivered yesterday afternoon and which
                    the Chargé was reliably informed is unlikely to be of tenor entirely
                    satisfactory to Bolivia.</p>
                <p>Department is telegraphing the Legation at Asuncion as follows:<anchor n="66"
                        xml:id="d568-f2"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“If note has not yet been delivered, please informally express the hope
                            that Paraguayan Government will take a conciliatory attitude and will do
                            nothing to disrupt relations with Bolivia. Now that the neutrals are
                            renewing the offer of good offices, it is very important that nothing
                            should be done to disturb the situation.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Please also informally endeavor to prevent a rupture of relations. You might
                    suggest as your own opinion to the Bolivian authorities that this is a matter
                    which might appropriately be referred to the neutral representatives in
                    Washington. Report developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
